INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - DAWN

A circular room of glass and brass. The great lens turns with a slow, hypnotic creak. Gulls cry outside.

OTTILIE BRANDVOLD (60s, keeper, oilskin, spyglass) stands at the rail. Across the room, HENRIETTA ASHDOWN-RAO (30s, inspector, crisp coat, leather satchel) opens her notebook.

HENRIETTA
Miss Brandvold, the log says the lamp went dark at three.

OTTILIE
It did.

HENRIETTA
For eleven minutes.

OTTILIE
For eleven minutes.

HENRIETTA
And you were here?

OTTILIE
I was asleep.

Henrietta lowers the notebook.

HENRIETTA
A keeper is not permitted to sleep.

OTTILIE
A keeper is not permitted to many things.

The lens turns. A shaft of pale light sweeps across both women's faces.

HENRIETTA
A ship went aground in those eleven minutes.

OTTILIE
(flat)
I know.

HENRIETTA
Forty lives.

Ottilie turns from the rail. Her hands are steady. Her face is not.

OTTILIE
Forty-one. I counted the cabin boy twice.

She sinks onto a stool. Henrietta waits, pen frozen.

OTTILIE (CONT'D)
Write it down. All of it.

Henrietta nods. She writes. Her hand shakes. The lens creaks. The light sweeps on.
